Technical Programme Manager, Security Engineering (Risk) &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the AI Security Institute&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI Security Institute is the world&#39;s largest and best-funded team dedicated to understanding advanced AI risks and translating that knowledge into action. We’re in the heart of the UK government with direct lines to No. 10 (the Prime Minister&#39;s office), and we work with frontier developers and governments globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re here because governments are critical for advanced AI going well, and UK AISI is uniquely positioned to mobilise them. With our resources, unique agility and international influence, this is the best place to shape both AI development and government action.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;vac_display_field_value&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The deadline for applying to this role is Wednesday 25th November 2026, end of day (UK Time).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the models we test get more capable and the environments we run them in get more sensitive, we have to continue to be able to run evaluations of highly capable models under proper control and ensure that it remains governed well. Building that governance and keeping it fast is what lets AISI keep pace with the work in front of it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Security Engineering team keeps AISI&#39;s research platform, evaluation environments, and sensitive data secure, and runs the governance, risk, and compliance around them. We harden the environments evaluations run in, detect and respond to threats, and build the controls that let evaluations of highly capable models proceed safely. We work with research teams across AISI, with partners in frontier AI companies and government.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rigorous safety governance and fast-moving research aren&#39;t mutually exclusive. AISI research involves working with highly capable AI models, often before they have been released to the public and often with lowered safeguards, to understand their true capabilities. That work has to be properly controlled, and someone has to build the processes and systems that help us make the call that it&#39;s safe to run without becoming a bottleneck. We&#39;re hiring a Technical Programme Manager in Security Engineering to own the AISI-wide governance mechanism that oversees these safety judgements, the controls research teams work under, and every edge case and escalation in between. You&#39;ll work with the team&#39;s engineers and the researchers whose work this governs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AISI-wide Governance Mechanism that oversees safety. &lt;/strong&gt;Own the process, make clear what it approves and how, help people work through their requirements proactively, and keep decisions well-evidenced and moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The research/control interface. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll own how research teams meet the security controls that apply to their work, and the defined path for handling the exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme architecture and delivery. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll track the team&#39;s work and spot problems early, with enough visibility to stay in control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-government governance engagement. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll represent AISI on governance and risk with partners across government, including the Cabinet Office, building the relationships, and turning departmental policy into AISI process.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may be a good fit if you have some of the following skills, experience and attitudes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record with technical colleagues. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve delivered technical programmes somewhere similarly ambiguous. You can scope and structure an open-ended goal. Technical teams trust you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort at the frontier of AI. &lt;/strong&gt;You don&#39;t have to be an ML researcher, but you need to hold your own in constant conversation with technical staff about the work, the strategy, and the risks. You should have a view on what&#39;s hard, what&#39;s speculative, what&#39;s blocked, and what &quot;good&quot; looks like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High agency and ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You own outcomes, not activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong prioritisation under pressure. &lt;/strong&gt;You can tell what actually matters day to day and quarter to quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong candidates may also have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in security, risk, or GRC. A technical background with a genuine interest in security is ideal but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in, or appetite for, modern productivity tools (coding agents, Linear, Slack) and AI tools as part of daily work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you don&#39;t meet every point above. We care more about what you&#39;ve broken, and how, than about certifications or job titles. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Selection process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The interview process may vary from vacancy to vacancy, however, you should expect a typical process to include some technical proficiency tests, discussions with a cross-section of our team at AISI (including non-technical staff) and conversations with your team lead. The process will culminate in a conversation with members of the senior leadership team here at AISI.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
