&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team and we welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. We value a wide range of perspectives and believe that our differences make us stronger.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering

Senior Garment Technologist &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT QUINCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quince is a destination for builders, creators, innovators, and operators who want to come together and challenge the status quo. Our mission is simple: make really high quality essentials for really low prices, fairly and sustainably. We deliver on that mission through a unique manufacturer-to-consumer (M2C) model eliminating the layers of traditional retail that add cost and result in consumers paying more than they need to. We find, build relationships with, and work directly with the manufacturing partners behind some of the world’s finest products. From there, our teams design smart, efficient operational processes&amp;nbsp; and build and deploy proprietary technology, AI, and analytics to help us scale fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What began with a small assortment of elevated basics has quickly grown into a cross-category brand spanning apparel, accessories, home goods, and more. Today, tens of millions of people across a growing number of countries come – and return – to Quince because they trust us to deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR CULTURE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quince is a culture built for builders by builders. Our way of working starts with a blank sheet of paper. We question conventional thinking, use technology and data to uncover new opportunities, and move quickly to turn ideas into reality. We aren’t interested in replicating how others do retail. We’re building a better way – at a speed and scale unlike anything that’s been done before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We dream big and chase the hard problems others shy away from. Rejecting long-held assumptions is part of our company&#39;s DNA.&amp;nbsp; Where conventional wisdom says you have to choose – soft or durable, speed or rigor, quality or price – we ask why that trade-off has to exist in the first place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our pace is fast and the bar is high because our customers expect a lot from us and we refuse to let them down. We believe the best results come from challenging ourselves, learning from one another, and building on each other&#39;s strengths.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Here, responsibility is not determined by role, tenure, or seniority. Every team member - no matter their level - has the opportunity to drive our business and shape our trajectory.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re someone who likes to imagine new possibilities and build better systems rather than plug-in to outdated ones, Quince is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2290&quot; data-local-id=&quot;6a0d0d38-3057-4834-9012-12f09f19e465&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;fabric-text-color-mark&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-text-custom-color=&quot;#0747a6&quot;&gt;&lt;u data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;THE ROLE &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2301&quot; data-local-id=&quot;6d5afd27-5970-45c1-b675-f5df64663cbf&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Garment Technologist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Garment Technologist&lt;/strong&gt; to join the founding team of Quince’s new London Design Atelier. In this role, you will own the technical execution, fit, construction, and consistency of ready-to-wear products across Women’s and Men’s, partnering closely with Design, Pattern Cutting, Product Development, Sourcing, Quality, and external manufacturing partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly hands-on role at the intersection of creative design and product execution. You will translate design intent into technically sound, production-ready garments, leading fittings, developing fit blocks and technical standards, and solving construction and pattern challenges throughout the development process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role means making fit, construction, and quality a competitive advantage for Quince — improving product consistency and customer satisfaction while reducing returns and enabling faster, more efficient product development as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical development and fit process from initial prototype through production approval across Women’s and Men’s RTW.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Design and Pattern Cutting to translate creative concepts into technically feasible, production-ready garments while preserving design intent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead fit sessions and provide clear, actionable fit, construction, and pattern comments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess garment proportions, balance, construction, finishing, and overall fit, recommending technical solutions where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and evolve fit blocks, grading standards, and technical standards across key product categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain accurate technical specifications, measurements, construction details, and fit documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review patterns and recommend pattern amendments to resolve fit, construction, and production issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Development, Sourcing, and Quality to ensure products meet Quince standards for fit, construction, quality, cost, and manufacturability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with external vendors and factories to troubleshoot technical challenges and ensure accurate execution of product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical risks early in development and drive solutions before production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer feedback, returns, product ratings, and other performance data to identify opportunities to improve fit and product execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish scalable technical development processes, standards, documentation, and ways of working for the London Atelier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global teams and vendors to ensure technical standards are consistently understood and executed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage digital and 3D development tools where appropriate to accelerate fittings, development, and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in garment technology, technical design, product engineering, or a closely related technical apparel role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong multi-product RTW experience, ideally across both Women’s and Men’s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical knowledge of garment construction, pattern cutting and amendments, grading, fit, fabrics, and production requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with tailoring and structured product, with the ability to technically assess complex garments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience owning the fit and technical development process from prototype through production approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly skilled in conducting fittings and translating observations into precise, actionable technical and pattern corrections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of technical specifications, measurements, tolerances, construction methods, and production standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with designers, pattern cutters, product developers, sourcing teams, factories, and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment with an exceptional eye for fit, proportion, construction, and detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using customer and product performance data to inform technical decisions and prioritize improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly hands-on, solutions-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple products and development timelines simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a premium, luxury, or highly design-led fashion environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in tailoring, outerwear, and other technically complex RTW categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and maintaining fit blocks and technical standards across multiple product categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with international vendors and manufacturing partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital pattern review, 3D fitting, or virtual product development tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping establish or evolve a technical function, pattern room, atelier, or product creation organization.&lt;/li&gt;
