Fullstack Web Developer &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Fullstack Web Developer to join our Web Apps team, in our Zürich office. In this role you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The web apps team plays a central role at Auterion and owns the systems that add connectivity and remote interfaces for fleet management and operations. Our services are responsible for ingesting and analyzing flight telemetry data, managing and updating the fleet as well as integrating with other systems across the stack.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across all the team’s web based projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate services between edge devices and our centralized services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle new feature discovery, prototyping and investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Customer Success team in debugging and resolving customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze user usage patterns and other statistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push initiatives to clean up, upgrade, and refactor existing services to reduce technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve integrations with 3rd party services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in a Fullstack web development or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with the Node.js&amp;nbsp; ecosystem, development and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with the Typescript ecosystem, development and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with modern SPAs (Vue.js ecosystem preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Postgres/SQL (queries, transactions, views, indexes, triggers) as well as ORM systems (Prisma)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Docker and container orchestration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with CI/CD pipelines (GoCD and GH Actions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monitoring and observability tools (Datadog, Grafana)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python proficiency is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CH/EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  Zurich

Senior Security Architect &lt;h1&gt;Senior Security Architect&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: London (Hybrid) | Practice Area: Technology &amp;amp; Engineering | Type: Permanent&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Shape secure technology architectures and safeguard the digital future of financial services and energy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the design of secure, resilient and scalable technology solutions that help financial institutions modernise their platforms, manage evolving cyber threats and deliver complex technology transformation with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Capco, you will play a pivotal role in shaping security architecture across some of our clients&#39; most complex and high-profile transformation programmes. Drawing on your expertise in security architecture, cloud technologies and modern security engineering, you will help organisations strengthen their security posture while enabling innovation and business growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with engineers, architects and senior stakeholders to design practical security solutions, evaluate architectural options and embed security into technology delivery. Your technical judgement, commercial awareness and ability to challenge assumptions constructively will help clients balance security, regulatory compliance, operational resilience and business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Security Architect, you will guide multidisciplinary teams, mentor colleagues and contribute to the development of Capco&#39;s Technology &amp;amp; Engineering Practice through technical leadership, knowledge sharing, delivery excellence and business development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the design and implementation of secure, scalable and resilient architectures across on-premises, cloud and hybrid environments, ensuring solutions align with business objectives, security standards and regulatory requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Shape security architecture strategies, technical standards and transformation roadmaps, evaluating architectural options, managing security risks and translating complex requirements into practical, maintainable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct threat modelling, security risk assessments and architectural reviews, defining appropriate security controls and remediation strategies while embedding Zero Trust principles and security-by-design practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guide the adoption of DevSecOps practices, integrating security controls throughout the software development lifecycle while collaborating with engineering, architecture and delivery teams to strengthen security outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explore and apply approved AI tools, automation and AI-enabled workflows to improve security architecture research, threat analysis, design documentation and delivery efficiency, maintaining appropriate human review, security controls, responsible AI governance and clear escalation pathways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven experience leading complex security architecture initiatives, translating business, technology and security requirements into practical, high-quality solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong architectural judgement and problem-solving capability, with the ability to evaluate security risks, challenge assumptions constructively and balance protection, resilience, usability and maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders, communicate complex security concepts clearly and influence technology and security decisions across business and engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working collaboratively across multidisciplinary technical teams, encouraging security awareness, knowledge sharing, engineering excellence and the professional development of colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commercial awareness and a client-focused mindset, with the ability to understand business objectives, identify opportunities for improvement and deliver measurable security and technology outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Essential Requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Security architecture across on-premises, cloud and hybrid environments: Proven experience designing and implementing secure architectures across complex technology estates, including cloud infrastructure, hybrid platforms and enterprise systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Security technologies and ecosystems: Experience designing solutions using Palo Alto, Microsoft or comparable security ecosystems, with a strong understanding of security architecture principles and their practical application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Security frameworks and Zero Trust Architecture: Deep knowledge of recognised security frameworks and standards, including NIST, ISO 27001, CAF and TOGAF, combined with experience designing and implementing Zero Trust Architecture solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Security engineering and risk management: Strong expertise across Identity and Access Management (IAM), endpoint protection, application security and network security, including threat modelling, security risk assessments and the definition of appropriate remediation strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DevSecOps and secure delivery: Experience embedding security controls into the software development lifecycle, applying DevSecOps principles and collaborating with engineering teams to support secure software and infrastructure delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Points For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relevant professional certifications, including CISSP, CISM, TOGAF or recognised cloud security certifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience defining AI security architectures, responsible AI governance frameworks, security guardrails or controls for AI-enabled systems, including Generative AI and Agentic AI, within regulated environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with security tooling, including Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) platforms, firewalls and Identity and Access Management solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience supporting regulatory compliance requirements, including GDPR and PCI-DSS, particularly within financial services or other regulated industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with programming languages such as Python, Java or C++, with the ability to understand how software engineering practices influence security architecture and technical delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Capco&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver high-impact technology solutions for Tier 1 financial institutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work in a collaborative, flat and entrepreneurial consulting culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Access continuous learning, training and industry certifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team shaping the future of digital financial services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help shape the future of digital transformation across financial services and energy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a competitive, people-first benefits package designed to support every aspect of your life:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Discretionary bonus, competitive pension, health insurance, life insurance and critical illness cover.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mental Health:&lt;/strong&gt; Easy access to CareFirst, Unmind, Aviva consultations, and in-house first aiders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family-Friendly:&lt;/strong&gt; Maternity, adoption, shared parental leave, plus paid leave for sickness, pregnancy loss, fertility treatment, menopause, and bereavement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family Care:&lt;/strong&gt; 8 complimentary backup care sessions for emergency childcare or elder care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holiday Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 weeks of annual leave with the option to buy or sell holiday days based on your needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Learning:&lt;/strong&gt; Your growth, your way – a minimum of 40 hours of training annually. Take your pick from workshops, certifications and e-learning. You&#39;ll also be assigned a Business Coach from Day One, offering one-on-one guidance to support your goals and accelerate your development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Healthcare Access:&lt;/strong&gt; Convenient online GP services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extra Perks:&lt;/strong&gt; Gympass (Wellhub), travel insurance, Tastecard, season ticket loans, Cycle to Work, and dental insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Inclusion at Capco&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to making our recruitment process accessible and straightforward for everyone. If you need any adjustments at any stage, just let us know – we’ll be happy to help. We value each person’s unique perspective and contribution. At Capco, we believe that being yourself is your greatest strength. Our #BeYourselfAtWork culture encourages individuality and collaboration – a mindset that shapes how we work with clients and each other every day.&lt;/p&gt;
